{"header":"<h1>Module <code><span>Private.Signal_fd</span></code></h1>","type":"documentation","uses_katex":false,"breadcrumbs":[{"name":"Index","href":"../../../../index.html","kind":"leaf-page"},{"name":"eio","href":"../../../index.html","kind":"page"},{"name":"Eio_unix","href":"../../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Private","href":"../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Signal_fd","href":"#","kind":"module"}],"toc":[],"source_anchor":null,"preamble":"","content":"<div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-t\"><a href=\"#type-t\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> t</span><span> = <span class=\"keyword\">private</span> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Unix</span>.file_descr</span></code></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-get_singleton\"><a href=\"#val-get_singleton\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> get_singleton : <span>unit <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <a href=\"#type-t\">t</a></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p><code>get_singleton ()</code> returns a file descriptor that becomes readable when a signal is received (for a <code>Signal_handle</code> handler installed by <a href=\"../../index.html#val-set_signal\"><code>Eio_unix.set_signal</code></a>).</p><p>Backends should monitor this FD so that they wake up and take the runtime lock when it is readable. This enables the signal to be processed promptly.</p><p>The FD is created lazily the first time the function is called and never closed.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-ack\"><a href=\"#val-ack\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> ack : <span><a href=\"#type-t\">t</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> unit</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p><code>ack t</code> reads one or more pending events from the FD. Call this when <code>t</code> becomes readable.</p></div></div>"}